// Generated by tools/fragments.ts from fragments/**/*.md (npm run fragments): edit the .md files, not this.
/** Every seed fragment's file, by its path under fragments/ without .md, in path order. */
export const SEED_FILES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "bands/01-band": "---\nid: band\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: band\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&band &drums &bass &pad &stab &lead\n&drums, &drumsOut from \"drums performer\" &drumlines\n&bass, &bassOut from \"bass performer\"(bassLevel=&bassLevel) &bassline\n&pad, &padOut from \"pad performer\"(padLevel=&padLevel) &padline\n&stab, &stabOut from \"stab performer\"(stabLevel=&stabLevel) &stabline\n&lead, &leadOut from \"lead performer\"(leadLevel=&leadLevel) &leadline\n&bassLevel map=amp .8\n&padLevel map=amp .8\n&stabLevel map=amp .8\n&leadLevel map=amp .8\n&bassV s=saw loop=C2 lpf=450..900 * &style[artic] lpq=4 env=&(map=adsr .005 .2 .7 .05)\n&leadV s=square loop=C4 lpf=1400..3600 * &style[energy] env=&(map=adsr .023 0 1 .08)\n&sound map=sample [&drumsOut, &bassOut * .8, &padOut * .35, &stabOut * .4, &leadOut * .45]\n&midi map=midi &leadOut &bassOut [&padOut, &stabOut] ~!6 &drumsOut\n```\n\nThe default band (decision 063 §1, #391): who plays a score, on what, and where it goes out. A score ends in `* from band`, the same line on every client, and each client's resolver answers `band` with its own; this is the one cells' library holds.\n\n**Its head, `&band`,** is decision 061's table of performers: the five role cells, `&drums`, `&bass`, `&pad`, `&stab` and `&lead`, so a score's selector over the band (`&form over=&band step=1m …`) reads the client's players. Who plays when is the score's; who they are, the band's.\n\n**The performers** are the seed library's five (decisions 058 and 061), each a copy taken by its signature (decision 065): its role and its gate, `&bass, &bassOut from \"bass performer\"(bassLevel=&bassLevel) &bassline`. The part each plays is the score's, by its interface name (`&drumlines`, `&bassline`, `&padline`, `&stabline`, `&leadline`), and so are its levels (`&bassLevel` …). A level the score doesn't write is the band's own, one level of .8, the performers' default; the score's line wins over it, as a piece's line wins over what it takes (decision 054 §2). A part the score doesn't write rests, and cells says so (decision 063 §4); a conductor that rests a role writes it as a tacet (`&padline step=1m ~`), and nothing is said.\n\n**The instruments** are the performers' own (`bass`, `keys`, `pad`, `lead`, and 13 of `gm_kit`'s voices), each with a sound, at the centre of style space. Two of them read the score's style, `&style` (decision 063 §3), where Jambot's `timbreOf` reads it (yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/sound.ts` @ 227aa74), as lines of the band, which win over the instrument it takes:\n- the bass's cutoff opens with articulation, from 450 Hz at legato to 900 Hz at staccato (`lpf=450..900 * &style[artic]`);\n- the lead's opens with energy, from 1400 Hz to 3600 Hz (`lpf=1400..3600 * &style[energy]`).\n\nJambot's other two readings don't move a cells voice: the lead's blend of a triangle and a square, and the chords' attack and release, are an envelope's times and a wave, written as numbers. The chords keep the centre's envelope at every style, and the lead its square.\n\n**Which instrument a performer plays at a style** is the band's choice, made by a query at resolution, not by a line: `resolveBand(score)` answers `band` with this text, each pitched voice replaced by the first instrument the library ranks at the score's style that defines it, where that isn't the performer's own (`bandAt`, `src/repository/band.ts`; yggi/jambot#527's rule, moved here). At each of Jambot's eight presets that is the performer's own instrument, so the band plays as written; at Electro swing's point the upright bass, the brass stab and the clarinet, at Spooky's the round bass, the organ, the celesta and the theremin (#366). Each holds its default's register, so MIDI out sends the same notes. A line can't make that choice: a voice reads a style as a moving parameter, and a wave or a set of envelopes is no such parameter.\n\n**The cards:** a sound card that hears every gate, the drums at full, the bass at .8, the lead at .45 and the chords under it (the pad at .35, the stab at .4), as Jambot's synth balances its parts (`PEAK`, yggi/jambot `apps/web/src/audio/voices.ts` @ 227aa74, its chords' several notes each quieter), and a MIDI card on Jambot's channels: 1 the lead, 2 the bass, 3 the pad and the stab, 10 the drums. A person with a fifth synth gives the stab its own channel in their band.\n\nA score played on this band sends the MIDI Jambot's section text sends on its single card (channel, note, velocity, onset and end): its twenty sections at the ten presets, seeds 1 and 2, 0 mismatched (`band.slow.test.ts`).\n\nAssociated once as the facet `band` at the centre of style space, at weight 1: it plays every style, reading the style it is given.\n",
  "bass/01-root-bass": "---\nid: root bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/bass.ts @ 1037a80\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=2n 0 0\n```\n\nJambot's bass pattern `root`: the root of the chord in force on one and on three, the bar's downbeat and its half (`bass.ts` weighs them 1 and 0.6).\nIts own lines read the host's `&harm` (`over=&harm`: each index a tone of the chord sounding) and tap the host's main meter, so it fits any workbench whose `&bar` and `&harm` are written first; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058), and the workbench's card sends it.\n\nAt the point where the root is all `bass.ts` plays: there its blend weighs the pump, the eighths and the funk line 0 (no sync, no energy, legato), so the root's share is 1.\nOf the points where it is 1, this is the nearest to Ambient's, the preset where the root's share is greatest (0.68): Ambient's harmony, its sync and energy at 0.\nIt is also at the three presets where the root is what `bass.ts` plays most, as the meters are at theirs (#209): Synth-pop's (0.32, the funk line 0.27), Deep house's (0.31, tied with the funk line, which the root takes as first in `bass.ts`'s order) and Ambient's (0.68). A preset plays a blend, and its nearest pattern's point needn't be the pattern it plays most.\n\nWhat `bass.ts` adds that a fixed line doesn't: on three it plays the fifth one section in five and an octave up one in four, by a draw per section and step; it thins the line by the energy (each step sounds when a held draw falls under its weight times 0.55 + 0.6 × energy); the octave, the voice leading and the velocity are the performer's.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"root bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"root bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "bass/02-pumping-bass": "---\nid: pumping bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/bass.ts @ 1037a80\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=8n ~ 0 ~ 0 ~ 0 ~ 0\n```\n\nJambot's bass pattern `pump`: the root of the chord in force on the eighth after each beat, and nothing on the beat, not even on a chord change (`bass.ts` plays the new root on a change only while the pump weighs under 0.45).\nIts own lines read the host's `&harm` and tap the host's main meter; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058), and the workbench's card sends it.\n\nAt the one point where the pump's share of `bass.ts`'s blend is greatest, 0.74: a static vamp, staccato, no sync (each a factor of the pump: `(1 − harm) × artic × (1 − sync)`), and no energy, which would bring in the eighths.\nThat is Techno's harmony and articulation, its sync and energy at 0.\nIt is also at Techno's, the preset where the pump is what `bass.ts` plays most (0.50), as the meters are at theirs (#209).\n\nWhat `bass.ts` adds that a fixed line doesn't: the fifth one step in five and an octave up one in four, by a draw per section and step; the thinning by the energy (here 0.55: each offbeat sounds about one section in two); the octave, the voice leading and the velocity, the performer's.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"pumping bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"pumping bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "bass/03-eighths-bass": "---\nid: eighths bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/bass.ts @ 1037a80\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=8n 0!8\n```\n\nJambot's bass pattern `eight`: the root of the chord in force on every eighth (`bass.ts` weighs the downbeat 1, the bar's half 0.9, the others 0.8).\nIts own lines read the host's `&harm` and tap the host's main meter; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058), and the workbench's card sends it.\n\nAt a point where the eighths' share of `bass.ts`'s blend is greatest, 0.63: full energy and no sync (the eighths weigh `0.6 × energy × (1 − funk)`, the funk line weighs the sync), and no pump (legato, or a harmony that moves fully).\nThe eighths are what `bass.ts` plays most at no preset, so unlike the others they sit at no preset's point (#209).\nTechno, the preset where their share is greatest (0.24), is as near two of those points (Techno legato, and Techno with its harmony moving), so it sits at the root bass's point with the energy at 1: there `bass.ts` moves from the root alone to the eighths by the energy alone.\n\nWhat `bass.ts` adds that a fixed line doesn't: the fifth one step in five and an octave up one in four, off the downbeat; the thinning by the energy (here 1.15: each eighth sounds but about one in twelve); the octave, the voice leading and the velocity, the performer's.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"eighths bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"eighths bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "bass/04-funk-bass": "---\nid: funk bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/bass.ts @ 1037a80\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=16n 0 ~ ~ 0 ~ ~ 0 0 ~ ~ 0 0 ~ &bassNext &bassNext ~\n&bassNext over=&harm[>>] 0\n```\n\nJambot's bass pattern `funk`, its line on 4/4's sixteen steps, every step it weighs (`bass.ts`'s `FUNK`: 1, 0.7, 0.8, 0.4, 0.7, 0.5, 0.3, 0.8): the root of the chord in force, and on the bar's last two sixteenths the next chord's root, anticipated (`&bassNext`, over `&harm[>>]`).\nIts own lines read the host's `&harm` and tap the host's main meter; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058), and the workbench's card sends it.\n\nAt Funk's point: there the funk line's share of `bass.ts`'s blend is the greatest it gets, 0.74 (full sync weighs it 1 and the pump and the eighths 0), and Funk is the preset where its share is greatest.\nIt is also at the two other presets where the funk line is what `bass.ts` plays most, as the meters are at theirs (#209): Lo-fi hip hop's (0.48) and Bossa nova's (0.63).\nAt full sync `bass.ts` anticipates the next chord nine times in ten on a step of the bar's last three that isn't a change (`0.9 × sync`), so this line plays the anticipation.\n\nWhat `bass.ts` adds that a fixed line doesn't: the tenth time, the root or the fifth there; the fifth one step in five and an octave up one in four elsewhere off the downbeat; the thinning by each step's weight and the energy (here 1: the 0.3 and the 0.4 sound about one section in three); the octave, the voice leading and the velocity, the performer's.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"funk bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"funk bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "bass/05-walking-bass": "---\nid: walking bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/bass.ts @ 1037a80\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=4n 0 1 2 &bassNext^$-1\n&bassNext over=&harm[>>] 0\n```\n\nJambot's bass pattern `walk`, a note on every beat: the root of the chord in force on one, its third and its fifth, and on the last beat the next chord's root a semitone below (`&bassNext^$-1`: the next chord's root, `over=&harm[>>]`, moved a step of the grid, a semitone).\nThe semitone can't be an index: over the chord in force an accidental moves a degree of the key, so `0b` over `&harm[>>]` is a semitone only where the key's degree below the next root is one.\nIts own lines read the host's `&harm` and tap the host's main meter; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058), and the workbench's card sends it.\n\nAt Swing jazz's point, under its meter swung on `8n` (`4/4 swung on 8n`): `bass.ts` walks only where the meter swings its eighths (`eighthSwing`) and the harmony moves (`harm ≥ 2/3`), and there the walk's share of its blend is the greatest it gets, 0.74, the funk line, the pump and the eighths all 0.\nThe swing is the meter's, not a style axis, so the point says only the harmony.\nSwing jazz is the only preset where the walk is what `bass.ts` plays most, and this point is Swing jazz's (#209); at the presets whose harmony moves but whose meter doesn't swing, the pattern played most is associated there and is found before the walk.\n\nWhat `bass.ts` draws that a fixed line chooses: the second and third beats each the third, the fifth or the seventh (the fifth twice over where the chord has none), a third each, so this line is one walk it plays, up through the chord; the approach from below or above, half each, so this one from below. Under a harmony that changes on the bar's half it leads into that change too. The octave, the voice leading and the velocity are the performer's.\nAlso at the point proposed for an Electro swing preset (#349), weight 1: the walk [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md) plays. It is placed by hand, not by `bass.ts`'s blend, which has no such preset.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"walking bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"walking bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "bass/06-creeping-bass": "---\nid: creeping bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: bass\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassline from &harm\n&bassline over=&harm step=4n 0@2 &creep^$1 0\n&creep over=&harm 0\n```\n\nA bass that creeps: the root of the chord in force held two beats, then a semitone above it, and back (`&creep^$1`: the root moved a step of the grid, a semitone, as the walking bass's approach moves `&bassNext`), the shark's two notes slowed to a walk on tiptoe.\nIts line reads the host's `&harm` and taps the host's main meter; it has no card (#291): it is the part the bass performer plays (`&bassline`, decision 058). It is four beats long, so in 5/4 it turns against the bar, the semitone landing a beat later each time round.\nWritten by hand for the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1, Jambot's to adopt (decision 041).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bassline from &harm`. `&bassline from \"creeping bass\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bassline from \"creeping bass\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "expression/01-vibrato": "---\nid: vibrato\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: expression\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&vibrato map=lin loop=5 0 .1 0 -.1 0\n```\n\nA singer's or a string player's vibrato (#196): the pitch rising a tenth of a semitone above the note and falling as far below, five times a second, a voice's `pitch=` (`&lead s=saw loop=C4 pitch=&vibrato`).\nIt is the vibrato the examples wrote out most, `pitch=&(map=lin loop=5 0 .1 0 -.1 0)` in bossa, BWV 847 and pop and near it in six more (five to six a second, eight to fifteen hundredths of a semitone), which take it from here.\nA drift that takes seconds to come round, a flutter, or a vibrato wider or slower on purpose is a piece's own: it writes its own cell, as spooky, baustelle and electroswing do.\n\nIt defines a cell and uses nothing, so it fits any workbench. Associated once, as the facet `expression`, at the centre of style space, at a quarter weight: what a voice does to its notes is no style's, and a query for an expression finds it there.\n",
  "expression/02-envelopes": "---\nid: envelopes\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: expression\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&click map=adsr 0 .03 0 .02\n&tap map=adsr 0 .08 0 .04\n&snap map=adsr 0 .12 0 .05\n&thump map=adsr 0 .3 0 .05\n&strike map=adsr .005 .15 .5 .05\n&pluck map=adsr .005 .25 .5 .1\n&swell map=adsr .02 .3 .5 .3\n```\n\nThe shapes a note's level takes, by name (#196): a voice's `env=` (`&hh s=white hpf=8000 env=&click`), each attack, decay, sustain and release in seconds and a level, as `map=adsr` reads them.\nThey are the seven the examples wrote out most, each from its most common spelling:\n- **Struck, nothing held:** `&click` (a hat, a rim, a tick, 30 ms), `&tap` (80 ms), `&snap` (a snare, 120 ms), `&thump` (a kick, 300 ms).\n- **Held:** `&strike` (a stab, struck and held at half), `&pluck` (a plucked string, a quarter second to half), `&swell` (a pad: a soft attack, a long release).\n\nAn envelope near one of them, each value within a fifth of it, became it in the examples (the owner, #196: \"collapse … minimal differences … as long as the 'spirit and style of the piece' is preserved\"); one that is a piece's own, slower, longer or shaped otherwise, stays as the piece writes it.\nThe names are no performer's (`&stab`, `&pad`, `&lead`, `&keys` are role cells, decision 061), so a piece that plays those parts takes these too.\n\nIt defines cells and uses nothing, so it fits any workbench. Associated once, as the facet `expression`, as `vibrato` is: at the centre of style space, at a quarter weight.\n",
  "forms/01-call-and-answer": "---\nid: call and answer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: form\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&phrase from (&answer) &call\n&phrase step=8n &call &answer\n&answer step=8n &call^-2\n```\n\nThe call and its answer: the call, then the call two degrees down, as blues and West African music answer a call, and as Jambot's lead lifts a line (an operator on the call, decision 052). Its hole is `&call`; `&answer` is its helper, an operator on the call by default, which a piece overrides by naming it (`use &phrase, &answer from \"call and answer\"`, decision 059).\nWith a one-bar call it is 2 bars, with a two-bar call 4.\nIt taps the host's meter by the eighth (`step=8n`), and a splice plays its whole line at the splicing braid's rate, so a motif written in eighths keeps its rhythm in it. It has no voice and no card (#291): the lead performer plays it as its `&leadline` (`&leadline step=8n &phrase`), or a piece splices it where it likes.\nAt the centre of style space, as the facet `form`, weight 1: a form fits any style, and a query for one finds them in this order.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&phrase from (&answer) &call`. `&phrase from \"call and answer\" &motif` takes a copy of it, `&call` its main argument; `&answer` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"call and answer\"(answer=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &phrase from \"call and answer\"`, it reads `&call` by name, as before.\n",
  "forms/02-sentence": "---\nid: sentence\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: form\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&sentence from (&continuation) &call\n&sentence step=8n &call &call^1 &continuation\n&continuation step=8n inverse(&call) &call[::-1]\n```\n\nCaplin's sentence: a presentation, the idea and the idea moved a degree up, then a continuation as long, here the idea mirrored (`inverse(&call)`) and the idea backwards (`&call[::-1]`), the material broken up as a continuation does. Its hole is `&call`; `&continuation` is its helper, a piece's to override by naming it.\nWith a one-bar call it is 4 bars, with a two-bar call 8.\nIt taps the host's meter by the eighth (`step=8n`), and a splice plays its whole line at the splicing braid's rate, so a motif written in eighths keeps its rhythm in it. It has no voice and no card (#291): the lead performer plays it as its `&leadline` (`&leadline step=8n &sentence`), or a piece splices it where it likes.\nAt the centre of style space, as the facet `form`, weight 1: a form fits any style, and a query for one finds them in this order.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&sentence from (&continuation) &call`. `&sentence from sentence &motif` takes a copy of it, `&call` its main argument; `&continuation` an optional parameter, its line its default (`sentence(continuation=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &sentence from sentence`, it reads `&call` by name, as before.\n",
  "forms/03-period": "---\nid: period\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: form\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&period from (&antecedent, &consequent) &call\n&period step=8n &antecedent &consequent\n&antecedent step=8n &call &call^1\n&consequent step=8n &call &call^-1\n```\n\nA period: an antecedent and a consequent, the same start, a different end. The antecedent ends a degree above the call (open), the consequent a degree below (closed). Its hole is `&call`; `&antecedent` and `&consequent` are its helpers, a piece's to override by naming them.\nWith a one-bar call it is 4 bars, with a two-bar call 8.\nIt taps the host's meter by the eighth (`step=8n`), and a splice plays its whole line at the splicing braid's rate, so a motif written in eighths keeps its rhythm in it. It has no voice and no card (#291): the lead performer plays it as its `&leadline` (`&leadline step=8n &period`), or a piece splices it where it likes.\nAt the centre of style space, as the facet `form`, weight 1: a form fits any style, and a query for one finds them in this order.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&period from (&antecedent, &consequent) &call`. `&period from period &motif` takes a copy of it, `&call` its main argument; `&antecedent`, `&consequent` optional parameters, their lines their defaults (`period(antecedent=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &period from period`, it reads `&call` by name, as before.\n",
  "forms/04-aaba": "---\nid: AABA\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: form\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&chorus from (&b) &a\n&chorus step=8n &a &a &b &a\n&b step=8n &a^3\n```\n\nThe thirty-two-bar song form, AABA, in its letters: an A three times, the bridge before the last. Its holes are `&a`, not `&call`, because an A is often a phrase itself (`&a step=8n &phrase`, the call and answer), and the bridge `&b` is its helper, A moved a fourth up by default, a piece's to override by naming it (`use &chorus, &b from AABA`).\nWith a one-bar A it is 4 bars, with a two-bar A 8.\nIt taps the host's meter by the eighth (`step=8n`), and a splice plays its whole line at the splicing braid's rate, so a motif written in eighths keeps its rhythm in it. It has no voice and no card (#291): the lead performer plays it as its `&leadline` (`&leadline step=8n &chorus`), or a piece splices it where it likes.\nAt the centre of style space, as the facet `form`, weight 1: a form fits any style, and a query for one finds them in this order.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&chorus from (&b) &a`. `&chorus from AABA &motif` takes a copy of it, `&a` its main argument; `&b` an optional parameter, its line its default (`AABA(b=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &chorus from AABA`, it reads `&a` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/01-tonic-vamp": "---\nid: tonic vamp\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/themes.ts @ 0a56da9\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=8 [0,2,4]!8\n```\n\nA vamp of Jambot's themes (`themes.ts`, `VAMPS`), eight bars over the host's key: the triad on the key's first degree for all eight bars: the vamp `[0]`, a stack of degrees `&key` reads (the chord in force a bass or a comp reads, `over=&harm`).\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nThe mode is the host key's, so one text is every mode's vamp that has these degrees: `aeolian`, `dorian`.\n\nThe layout is `buildTheme`'s under harm 0.15, one chord per four bars: the first four bars the vamp's first chord, the second four its second (`chords[1 % n]`, the first again for a vamp of one).\nFrom 0.15 to 0.33 it lays the same chords two bars each, twice over (`[0, 0, c, c]`), and over 0.33 it walks the mode's transition table instead, which stays Jambot's generator on a miss.\n\nAt the points where `buildTheme` plays it: aeolian at Techno's point; dorian at Funk's point. A mode's vamps are drawn alike (`next() · vamps.length`), so each weighs 1, and a query for the harmony at a mode's point finds all of that mode's vamps at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"tonic vamp\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"tonic vamp\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/02-vamp-to-the-seventh": "---\nid: vamp to the seventh\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/themes.ts @ 0a56da9\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=8 [0,2,4]!4 [6,8,10]!4\n```\n\nA vamp of Jambot's themes (`themes.ts`, `VAMPS`), eight bars over the host's key: the triad on the key's first degree for four bars, then the one on its seventh (degree 6) for four: the vamp `[0, 6]`, a stack of degrees `&key` reads (the chord in force a bass or a comp reads, `over=&harm`).\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nThe mode is the host key's, so one text is every mode's vamp that has these degrees: `aeolian`, `dorian`, `mixolydian`. No preset of Jambot's is mixolydian, so mixolydian gives it no point of its own.\n\nThe layout is `buildTheme`'s under harm 0.15, one chord per four bars: the first four bars the vamp's first chord, the second four its second (`chords[1 % n]`, the first again for a vamp of one).\nFrom 0.15 to 0.33 it lays the same chords two bars each, twice over (`[0, 0, c, c]`), and over 0.33 it walks the mode's transition table instead, which stays Jambot's generator on a miss.\n\nAt the points where `buildTheme` plays it: aeolian at Techno's point; dorian at Funk's point. A mode's vamps are drawn alike (`next() · vamps.length`), so each weighs 1, and a query for the harmony at a mode's point finds all of that mode's vamps at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"vamp to the seventh\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"vamp to the seventh\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/03-vamp-to-the-fourth": "---\nid: vamp to the fourth\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/themes.ts @ 0a56da9\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=8 [0,2,4]!4 [3,5,7]!4\n```\n\nA vamp of Jambot's themes (`themes.ts`, `VAMPS`), eight bars over the host's key: the triad on the key's first degree for four bars, then the one on its fourth (degree 3) for four: the vamp `[0, 3]`, a stack of degrees `&key` reads (the chord in force a bass or a comp reads, `over=&harm`).\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nThe mode is the host key's, so one text is every mode's vamp that has these degrees: `aeolian`, `dorian`, `ionian`, `mixolydian`. No preset of Jambot's is mixolydian, so mixolydian gives it no point of its own.\n\nThe layout is `buildTheme`'s under harm 0.15, one chord per four bars: the first four bars the vamp's first chord, the second four its second (`chords[1 % n]`, the first again for a vamp of one).\nFrom 0.15 to 0.33 it lays the same chords two bars each, twice over (`[0, 0, c, c]`), and over 0.33 it walks the mode's transition table instead, which stays Jambot's generator on a miss.\n\nAt the points where `buildTheme` plays it: aeolian at Techno's point; dorian at Funk's point; ionian at Ambient's point with its harmony at 0.12. A mode's vamps are drawn alike (`next() · vamps.length`), so each weighs 1, and a query for the harmony at a mode's point finds all of that mode's vamps at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"vamp to the fourth\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"vamp to the fourth\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/04-vamp-to-the-sixth": "---\nid: vamp to the sixth\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/themes.ts @ 0a56da9\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=8 [0,2,4]!4 [5,7,9]!4\n```\n\nA vamp of Jambot's themes (`themes.ts`, `VAMPS`), eight bars over the host's key: the triad on the key's first degree for four bars, then the one on its sixth (degree 5) for four: the vamp `[0, 5]`, a stack of degrees `&key` reads (the chord in force a bass or a comp reads, `over=&harm`).\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nThe mode is the host key's, so one text is every mode's vamp that has these degrees: `aeolian`, `ionian`.\n\nThe layout is `buildTheme`'s under harm 0.15, one chord per four bars: the first four bars the vamp's first chord, the second four its second (`chords[1 % n]`, the first again for a vamp of one).\nFrom 0.15 to 0.33 it lays the same chords two bars each, twice over (`[0, 0, c, c]`), and over 0.33 it walks the mode's transition table instead, which stays Jambot's generator on a miss.\n\nAt the points where `buildTheme` plays it: aeolian at Techno's point; ionian at Ambient's point with its harmony at 0.12. A mode's vamps are drawn alike (`next() · vamps.length`), so each weighs 1, and a query for the harmony at a mode's point finds all of that mode's vamps at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"vamp to the sixth\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"vamp to the sixth\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/05-vamp-to-the-fifth": "---\nid: vamp to the fifth\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/themes.ts @ 0a56da9\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=8 [0,2,4]!4 [4,6,8]!4\n```\n\nA vamp of Jambot's themes (`themes.ts`, `VAMPS`), eight bars over the host's key: the triad on the key's first degree for four bars, then the one on its fifth (degree 4) for four: the vamp `[0, 4]`, a stack of degrees `&key` reads (the chord in force a bass or a comp reads, `over=&harm`).\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nThe mode is the host key's, so one text is every mode's vamp that has these degrees: `ionian`.\n\nThe layout is `buildTheme`'s under harm 0.15, one chord per four bars: the first four bars the vamp's first chord, the second four its second (`chords[1 % n]`, the first again for a vamp of one).\nFrom 0.15 to 0.33 it lays the same chords two bars each, twice over (`[0, 0, c, c]`), and over 0.33 it walks the mode's transition table instead, which stays Jambot's generator on a miss.\n\nAt the points where `buildTheme` plays it: ionian at Ambient's point with its harmony at 0.12. A mode's vamps are drawn alike (`next() · vamps.length`), so each weighs 1, and a query for the harmony at a mode's point finds all of that mode's vamps at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"vamp to the fifth\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"vamp to the fifth\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "harmony/06-dark-cadence": "---\nid: dark cadence\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: harmony\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&harm from &key\n&harm over=&key step=1m cycle=4 [0,2,4] [5,7,9] [3,5,7] [4,6,8]\n```\n\nFour bars over the host's key, a chord a bar: the tonic, the sixth, the fourth, the fifth (i, ♭VI, iv, V in a minor key), then round again, the fifth pulling back to the tonic.\nIn harmonic minor, the key the point finds, the fifth is major (A C♯ E over D), a dominant, and the sixth (B♭ D F) sits a semitone above the fifth's root, so the bass falls B♭, G, A and the chords lean in by semitones.\nIt defines `&harm` and uses the host's `&key` and main meter, so it fits any workbench that writes those first; it has no card, and plays only through what reads it.\nIts lap is four bars, not the vamps' eight: Jambot's composer reads only progressions of eight (yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/harmony-query.ts`), so it doesn't take this one yet, and where no harmony is near one of its presets (Synth-pop, Deep house, Lo-fi hip hop, Bossa nova, Swing jazz) it generates its harmony as before, though this is the nearest there.\nWritten by hand for the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1, Jambot's to adopt (decision 041).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&harm from &key`. `&harm from \"dark cadence\" &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &harm from \"dark cadence\"`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "instruments/01-gm-kit": "---\nid: gm_kit\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&acousticbassdrum s=sine loop=G1 pitch=0..24 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .4 0 .05)\n&bd s=sine loop=A1 pitch=0..30 * &(map=adsr 0 .04 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .3 0 .05)\n&rim s=sine loop=E5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .03 0 .02)\n&sd s=white hpf=1500 env=&(map=adsr 0 .12 0 .05)\n&cp s=white hpf=1000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .08 0 .05)\n&electricsnare s=white hpf=2500 env=&(map=adsr 0 .09 0 .04)\n&lt s=sine loop=G2 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .25 0 .05)\n&hh s=white hpf=8000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .04 0 .02)\n&highfloortom s=sine loop=A2 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .23 0 .05)\n&ph s=white hpf=9000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .03 0 .01)\n&mt s=sine loop=C3 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .2 0 .05)\n&oh s=white hpf=7000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .25 0 .1)\n&lowmidtom s=sine loop=D3 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .18 0 .05)\n&ht s=sine loop=F3 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .15 0 .05)\n&cr s=white hpf=5000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .8 0 .3)\n&hightom s=sine loop=A3 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr 0 .05 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .13 0 .05)\n&rd s=white hpf=9000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .4 0 .2)\n&chinesecymbal s=white hpf=3000 distort=.3 env=&(map=adsr 0 .6 0 .2)\n&ridebell s=tri loop=E6 env=&(map=adsr 0 .5 0 .2)\n&tb s=white hpf=6000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .15 0 .05)\n&splashcymbal s=white hpf=6000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .35 0 .1)\n&cb s=square loop=G5 lpf=2500 env=&(map=adsr 0 .1 0 .03)\n&crashcymbaltwo s=white hpf=4000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .9 0 .3)\n&vibraslap s=white hpf=2000 crush=6 env=&(map=adsr 0 .6 0 .2)\n&ridecymbaltwo s=white hpf=8000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .5 0 .2)\n&hibongo s=sine loop=E4 pitch=0..7 * &(map=adsr 0 .02 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .1 0 .03)\n&lowbongo s=sine loop=A3 pitch=0..7 * &(map=adsr 0 .02 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .12 0 .03)\n&mutehiconga s=sine loop=C4 env=&(map=adsr 0 .05 0 .02)\n&openhiconga s=sine loop=C4 pitch=0..5 * &(map=adsr 0 .03 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .2 0 .05)\n&lowconga s=sine loop=G3 pitch=0..5 * &(map=adsr 0 .03 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .25 0 .05)\n&hightimbale s=tri loop=D5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .15 0 .05)\n&lowtimbale s=tri loop=A4 env=&(map=adsr 0 .18 0 .05)\n&highagogo s=tri loop=A5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .2 0 .05)\n&lowagogo s=tri loop=E5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .2 0 .05)\n&cabasa s=white hpf=5000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .06 0 .03)\n&sh s=white hpf=4000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .04 0 .03)\n&shortwhistle s=sine loop=B6 env=&(map=adsr .01 .08 0 .03)\n&longwhistle s=sine loop=B6 env=&(map=adsr .01 .1 .8 .1)\n&shortguiro s=white hpf=2500 lpf=5000 crush=4 env=&(map=adsr 0 .08 0 .02)\n&longguiro s=white hpf=2500 lpf=5000 crush=4 env=&(map=adsr 0 .3 0 .05)\n&claves s=sine loop=D7 env=&(map=adsr 0 .06 0 .03)\n&hiwoodblock s=sine loop=G5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .04 0 .02)\n&lowwoodblock s=sine loop=C5 env=&(map=adsr 0 .05 0 .02)\n&mutecuica s=sine loop=A4 pitch=0..7 * &(map=adsr 0 .08 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .1 0 .03)\n&opencuica s=sine loop=A4 pitch=0..12 * &(map=adsr .05 .2 0 0) env=&(map=adsr 0 .3 0 .05)\n&mutetriangle s=sine loop=A6 env=&(map=adsr 0 .08 0 .03)\n&opentriangle s=sine loop=A6 env=&(map=adsr 0 1.2 0 .4)\n```\n\nGeneral MIDI's drum kit (decision 054, #225): a voice for each of its 47 percussion notes, 35 to 81, in General MIDI's order, each under its kit name (`GM_KIT` in `src/engine/midi.ts`), so MIDI out sends each on its own note.\nThe names are Strudel's short names where Strudel has one (`&bd`, `&sd`, `&hh`, `&oh`, `&cp`, `&rim`, `&lt`, `&mt`, `&ht`, `&cr`, `&rd`, `&cb`, `&tb`, `&sh`), else General MIDI's, spelled as one word (`&lowmidtom`, `&crashcymbaltwo`); General MIDI's names for the first are aliases (`kick`, `cowbell`), which name the same note.\n\nIt defines voices and uses nothing, so it fills the holes a groove leaves (`&bd &sd &hh`), fits any workbench, and sounds only what a piece plays through it. Each sound is a first pass in cells' own parameters: a sine dropping in pitch for the drums and toms, filtered noise for the snares, hats and cymbals, a tuned sine or triangle for the hand percussion.\nA piece takes the voices it needs by name, so a groove need not bring in 47: `use &bd, &sd, &hh from gm_kit`. The drummer takes 13 so (`drums performer`); a kit of its own, the core kit, did that before `use` could name what it takes, and is retired (#196).\n\nA kit is style-neutral: it is associated once, as the facet `instrument`, at the centre of style space (every axis at 0.5), the point nearest the farthest preset, at weight 1, so a query for an instrument finds it first.\n",
  "instruments/03-bass": "---\nid: bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassV s=saw loop=C2 lpf=675 lpq=4 env=&(map=adsr .005 .2 .7 .05)\n```\n\nThe voice the bass lines play through (decision 054, rung 7's first; #244): `&bassV`, whose `loop=C2` sets the register, so the lines' MIDI notes on Jambot's bass channel are the notes they were when each line carried its own `&bassV loop=C2`.\nIts sound is Jambot's bass at the centre of style space (`timbreOf`, yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/sound.ts` @ 227aa74, and the synth that plays it, `apps/web/src/audio/voices.ts`): a saw through a resonant low-pass (`lpq=4`) at 675 Hz, where Jambot's opens from 450 Hz at legato to 900 Hz at staccato, struck with a short attack and held (#391). The default band's own `&bassV` reads the style for its cutoff (`lpf=450..900 * &style[artic]`, the fragment `band`); this one holds the centre's, so a text that names no style plays it.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1): a wave, a filter and an envelope. A sound changes no note it sends: MIDI out sends the notes it sent with no sound, and a MIDI card alone says the sound isn't sent (decision 064).\nIt defines the one voice the five bass lines read and uses nothing, so it fills their hole on any workbench; the lines no longer carry a voice of their own.\n\nAssociated as the kit is, once as the facet `instrument` at the centre of style space, at a quarter of its weight, so a query for an instrument finds the kit first; the composer asks for the bass by its id.\n",
  "instruments/04-keys": "---\nid: keys\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&keysV s=tri loop=C3 env=&(map=adsr .155 0 1 .41)\n```\n\nThe voice Jambot's comp plays its stabs through, and any keyboard part: `&keysV`, whose `loop=C3` sets the register, where Jambot's section text sounds its comp (`PIN_VOICES.comp`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so a stab played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends today, with no move on its gate.\nIts sound is Jambot's chords at the centre of style space (`timbreOf`, yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/sound.ts` @ 227aa74): a triangle that swells in over .155 s and dies over .41 s, where Jambot's attack shortens from .3 s at legato to .01 s at staccato and its release from .7 s to .12 s (#391). An envelope's times are numbers, not a moving parameter, so the default band plays this one at every style; a text that wants the staccato end writes its own `&keysV`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1), and changes no note MIDI out sends.\nIts register is its own (decision 058): a performer that plays it higher or lower says so on its gate (`play=&part^$12`).\n\nAssociated as `bass` is, once as the facet `instrument` at the centre of style space, at a quarter of the kit's weight; a performer asks for it by its id.\n",
  "instruments/05-pad": "---\nid: pad\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&padV s=tri loop=C3 env=&(map=adsr .155 0 1 .41)\n```\n\nThe voice Jambot's pad plays through: `&padV`, whose `loop=C3` sets the register, where Jambot's section text sounds its comp, pad and stab alike (`PIN_VOICES.comp`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so a pad played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends today, with no move on its gate. It is a voice of its own beside `keys`, though the two sit at one register, so a sound given to one (a pad's slow attack) isn't the other's.\nIts sound is the one Jambot gives its pad and its stab alike at the centre of style space (`timbreOf`, yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/sound.ts` @ 227aa74): a triangle that swells in over .155 s and dies over .41 s, as `keys` does (#391); a band that wants its pad slower than its stabs gives it its own envelope.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1), and changes no note MIDI out sends.\nIts register is its own (decision 058): a performer that plays it higher or lower says so on its gate (`play=&part^$12`).\n\nAssociated as `bass` is, once as the facet `instrument` at the centre of style space, at a quarter of the kit's weight; a performer asks for it by its id.\n",
  "instruments/06-lead": "---\nid: lead\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 0.25\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&leadV s=square loop=C4 lpf=2500 env=&(map=adsr .023 0 1 .08)\n```\n\nThe voice Jambot's lead plays through: `&leadV`, whose `loop=C4` sets the register, where Jambot's section text sounds its lead (`PIN_VOICES.lead`, E35's C4: yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so a lead played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends today, with no move on its gate.\nIts sound is Jambot's lead at the centre of style space (`timbreOf`, yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/sound.ts` @ 227aa74): a square through a low-pass at 2500 Hz, where Jambot's opens from 1400 Hz with no energy to 3600 Hz at full, with an attack of 23 ms (#391). The default band's own `&leadV` reads the style for its cutoff (`lpf=1400..3600 * &style[energy]`, the fragment `band`). Jambot's lead also moves from a soft triangle to a bright square as articulation rises, a blend of two waves in one voice, which a cells voice doesn't move: it is a square at every style.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1), and changes no note MIDI out sends.\nIts register is its own (decision 058): a performer that plays it higher or lower says so on its gate (`play=&part^$12`).\n\nAssociated as `bass` is, once as the facet `instrument` at the centre of style space, at a quarter of the kit's weight; a performer asks for it by its id.\n",
  "instruments/07-upright-bass": "---\nid: upright bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassV s=saw loop=C2 lpf=700 env=&(map=adsr .005 .3 .25 .08)\n```\n\nElectro swing's bass, plucked and dark: a saw closed down to 700 Hz with a short decay and a low sustain, so each note thumps and fades as a slapped string does.\nIt defines `&bassV`, the voice the bass performer plays (`use &bassV from bass`), so it fills the same hole as the default `bass` and can stand in for it.\nIt is [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md)'s `&bassV` but for its register: `loop=C2`, the default instrument's, so a bass line played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `bass` (the example's `loop=C3` is the piece's own).\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1): a wave, a low-pass filter and an envelope.\n\nAssociated at Electro swing's point (`ELECTRO_SWING`: sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/08-brass-stab": "---\nid: brass stab\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&keysV s=saw loop=C3 lpf=1800 env=&(map=adsr .01 .12 .25 .1)\n```\n\nElectro swing's stabs, a short brassy chord: a saw opened to 1800 Hz, a fast attack and a quick fall to a low sustain, so the Charleston's chords bite and get out of the way.\nIt defines `&keysV`, the voice the stab performer plays (`use &keysV from keys`), so it fills the same hole as the default `keys`.\nIt is [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md)'s `&keysV` word for word, at the default's register (`loop=C3`), so a stab played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `keys`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Electro swing's point (`ELECTRO_SWING`: sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/09-clarinet": "---\nid: clarinet\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&leadV s=square loop=C4 lpf=2400 env=&(map=adsr .02 .2 .7 .15) pitch=&(map=lin loop=5.5 0 .12 0 -.12 0)\n```\n\nElectro swing's lead: a square wave, the odd harmonics a clarinet's bore gives, softened by a low-pass at 2400 Hz, with a breath of attack and a vibrato of an eighth of a semitone five and a half times a second.\nIt defines `&leadV`, the voice the lead performer plays (`use &leadV from lead`), so it fills the same hole as the default `lead`.\nIt is [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md)'s `&leadV` word for word, at the default's register (`loop=C4`), so a line played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `lead`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1): a wave, a filter, an envelope and a pitch's shape.\n\nAssociated at Electro swing's point (`ELECTRO_SWING`: sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/10-muted-trumpet": "---\nid: muted trumpet\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&leadV s=saw loop=C4 lpf=1400 lpq=6 env=&(map=adsr .03 .1 .6 .12) pitch=&(map=lin loop=4.5 0 .08 0 -.08 0)\n```\n\nElectro swing's second lead, the trumpet with a mute in it: a saw through a resonant low-pass (1400 Hz, `lpq=6`), the mute's nasal peak, with a slower, narrower vibrato than the clarinet's.\nIt defines `&leadV`, the voice the lead performer plays, so it is the other instrument a lead player at this point may take; at the point the two are equally near, and a query lists the clarinet first, by id. A piece with both, as the example, gives the second player a voice of its own.\nIt is [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md)'s `&trumpetV`, named for the hole it fills, at the default lead's register (`loop=C4`), so a line played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `lead`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Electro swing's point (`ELECTRO_SWING`: sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/11-round-bass": "---\nid: round bass\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/spooky.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&bassV s=tri loop=C2 lpf=500 env=&(map=adsr .01 .3 .6 .2)\n```\n\nSpooky's bass, soft and round under the creep: a triangle closed down to 500 Hz, with a held sustain and a slow release, so the root and the semitone above it blur into each other.\nIt defines `&bassV`, the voice the bass performer plays (`use &bassV from bass`), so it fills the same hole as the default `bass`.\nIt is [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md)'s `&bassV` but for its register: `loop=C2`, the default instrument's, so a bass line played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `bass` (the example's `loop=C3` is the piece's own).\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Spooky's point (`SPOOKY`: sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/12-organ": "---\nid: organ\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/spooky.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&padV s=square loop=C3 lpf=1100 env=&(map=adsr .25 .2 .8 .6)\n```\n\nSpooky's pad, a church organ in an empty nave: a square, the reedy stop, filtered to 1100 Hz, swelling in over a quarter of a second and hanging on after the chord is let go.\nIt defines `&padV`, the voice the pad performer plays (`use &padV from pad`), so it fills the same hole as the default `pad`.\nIt is [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md)'s `&padV` word for word, at the default's register (`loop=C3`), so a chord played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `pad`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Spooky's point (`SPOOKY`: sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/13-theremin": "---\nid: theremin\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/spooky.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&leadV s=sine loop=C4 env=&(map=adsr .15 .2 .9 .4) pitch=&(map=lin loop=5 0 .25 0 -.25 0)\n```\n\nSpooky's lead, the theremin of a hundred horror films: a pure sine, fading in and out as a hand nears and leaves the antenna, with a wide vibrato of a quarter of a semitone five times a second.\nIt defines `&leadV`, the voice the lead performer plays (`use &leadV from lead`), so it fills the same hole as the default `lead`.\nIt is [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md)'s `&leadV` word for word, at the default's register (`loop=C4`), so a line played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `lead`.\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Spooky's point (`SPOOKY`: sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "instruments/14-celesta": "---\nid: celesta\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 0.125\n    facet: instrument\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/spooky.md @ 6d1bfa7\n---\n\n```cells\n&keysV s=sine loop=C3 env=&(map=adsr .002 .7 0 .5)\n```\n\nSpooky's bell, a celesta's struck tone: a sine that starts at once and dies away over most of a second with nothing held, the music box in the attic.\nIt defines `&keysV`, the voice the stab performer plays (`use &keysV from keys`), so it fills the same hole as the default `keys`.\nIt is [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md)'s `&keysV` but for its register: `loop=C3`, the default instrument's, so a stab played on it sends the MIDI notes it sends on `keys`. The example plays it at `loop=C5`, where a celesta sits; a player who wants it there says so on its gate (`play=&stabline^$24`, decision 058).\nIt sounds within the renderer's first stage (decision 062, R1).\n\nAssociated at Spooky's point (`SPOOKY`: sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; yggi/jambot#517) as the facet `instrument`, at half the default instruments' weight (0.125), so a query for an instrument finds it first at that point, and the kit and the defaults first at each of the eight presets (#350).\n",
  "meters/01-4-4": "---\nid: 4/4\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nStraight 4/4, at the points of the three presets that play straight: Synth-pop's, Techno's and Bossa nova's (yggi/jambot#360).\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/02-4-4-swung-on-8n": "---\nid: 4/4 swung on 8n\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from (&swing) &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo swing=&swing\n&swing swing=8n:2/3\n```\n\nJambot's swing 1: the triplet swing, 2/3, on the eighths; the sixteenths straight. At Swing jazz's point. A meter swung on `8n` brings in Jambot's jazz kit (yggi/jambot#360).\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nIts swing is its own, `&swing swing=8n:2/3`, a cell that is a swing alone (#308), which the meter reads (`swing=&swing`): a helper `use &bar from …` takes with it, and a text that swings otherwise names it to override it (`use &bar, &swing from …` and its own `&swing swing=8n:free(.64, .5..0.75)`, decision 059).\nAlso at the point proposed for an Electro swing preset (sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75; #349), weight 1: the meter [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md) plays, there with its own lighter swing, .64. Without it a query there finds 10/8.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from (&swing) &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4 swung on 8n\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument; `&swing` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"4/4 swung on 8n\"(swing=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4 swung on 8n\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/03-4-4-leaning-on-16n": "---\nid: 4/4 leaning on 16n\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from (&swing) &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo swing=&swing\n&swing swing=16n:.65\n```\n\nJambot's swing .45: the sixteenths' heaviest lean of the presets. At Lo-fi hip hop's point.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nIts swing is its own, `&swing swing=16n:.65`, a cell that is a swing alone (#308), which the meter reads (`swing=&swing`): a helper `use &bar from …` takes with it, and a text that swings otherwise names it to override it (`use &bar, &swing from …` and its own `&swing swing=8n:free(.64, .5..0.75)`, decision 059).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from (&swing) &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4 leaning on 16n\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument; `&swing` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"4/4 leaning on 16n\"(swing=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4 leaning on 16n\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/04-4-4-leaning-lightly-on-16n": "---\nid: 4/4 leaning lightly on 16n\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from (&swing) &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo swing=&swing\n&swing swing=16n:.6\n```\n\nJambot's swing .3. At Deep house's and Funk's points, whose swing is the same.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nIts swing is its own, `&swing swing=16n:.6`, a cell that is a swing alone (#308), which the meter reads (`swing=&swing`): a helper `use &bar from …` takes with it, and a text that swings otherwise names it to override it (`use &bar, &swing from …` and its own `&swing swing=8n:free(.64, .5..0.75)`, decision 059).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from (&swing) &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4 leaning lightly on 16n\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument; `&swing` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"4/4 leaning lightly on 16n\"(swing=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4 leaning lightly on 16n\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/05-4-4-leaning-faintly-on-16n": "---\nid: 4/4 leaning faintly on 16n\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from (&swing) &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo swing=&swing\n&swing swing=16n:31/60\n```\n\nJambot's swing .05: 31/60, an onset a thirtieth of a sixteenth late. At Ambient's point.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nIts swing is its own, `&swing swing=16n:31/60`, a cell that is a swing alone (#308), which the meter reads (`swing=&swing`): a helper `use &bar from …` takes with it, and a text that swings otherwise names it to override it (`use &bar, &swing from …` and its own `&swing swing=8n:free(.64, .5..0.75)`, decision 059).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from (&swing) &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4 leaning faintly on 16n\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument; `&swing` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"4/4 leaning faintly on 16n\"(swing=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4 leaning faintly on 16n\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/06-4-4-alla-breve": "---\nid: 4/4 alla breve\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0.9\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"4/4\") step=&tempo beat=2\n```\n\nAlla breve: the bpm counts half notes; fast, bright, marching.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"4/4 alla breve\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"4/4 alla breve\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/07-2-4": "---\nid: 2/4\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.1\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"2/4\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nA march, a polka: on the beat, plain, short and dense.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"2/4\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"2/4\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/08-3-4": "---\nid: 3/4\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.7\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.43\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"3/4\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nA waltz, a ballad: on the beat, rich, sparse.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nAlso near the point proposed for a Spooky preset (#349), 0.08 above it in energy, weight 1: the dance of the dead, a waltz, which the ladder fetches near `5/4`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"3/4\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"3/4\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/09-6-8": "---\nid: 6/8\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.2\n      artic: 0.2\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.27\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"6/8\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nA lilt: plain and sparse.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nAlso near the point proposed for a Spooky preset (#349), 0.08 below it in energy, weight 1: the slow lilt of a lullaby gone wrong, which the ladder fetches near `5/4`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"6/8\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"6/8\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/10-12-8": "---\nid: 12/8\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.7\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"12/8\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nA slow blues, a soul ballad: legato, off the beat.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"12/8\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"12/8\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/11-5-4": "---\nid: 5/4\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.4\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.3\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"5/4\") step=&tempo\n```\n\nCool jazz: rich, unhurried.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\nAlso at the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1: the meter of [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md), five beats that never settle, as a horror film's theme counts them. `6/8` and `3/4` sit near it (0.08 off, less and more energy), for the ladder to fetch.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"5/4\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"5/4\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/12-7-8": "---\nid: 7/8\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.8\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"7/8\") step=&tempo\n```\n\n3+2+2, a Balkan dance: off the beat, short and dense.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"7/8\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"7/8\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "meters/13-10-8": "---\nid: 10/8\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.6\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.8\n      energy: 0.9\n    weight: 1\n    facet: meter\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bar from &tempo\n&bar meter(\"10/8\") step=&tempo\n```\n\n3+2+3+2.\nIts tempo is the text's: `step=&tempo` reads a cell the text that uses it writes, a rate alone (`&tempo step=104bpm`, #290).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bar from &tempo`. `&bar from \"10/8\" 120bpm` takes a copy of it, `&tempo` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bar from \"10/8\"`, it reads `&tempo` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/01-aeolian": "---\nid: aeolian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(aeolian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe natural minor: the key Jambot's composer plays at Synth-pop's, Techno's and Lo-fi hip hop's points (`PRESETS`' `mode`, yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/style.ts), and the mode it opens in (`INITIAL_KEY`, A aeolian).\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic D`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole: there is no default, since a default tonic plays a wrong key silently (#117); the performer's room, `free(…)`, is the tonic cell's to give (`&tonic free(…)`, not yet a form).\n\nAt the point of each preset that plays it, weight 1, so a query for the mode at one of them finds aeolian first, at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from aeolian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from aeolian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/02-dorian": "---\nid: dorian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(dorian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe minor with a major sixth: the key Jambot's composer plays at Deep house's and Funk's points (`PRESETS`' `mode`, yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/style.ts).\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic D`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole: there is no default, since a default tonic plays a wrong key silently (#117); the performer's room, `free(…)`, is the tonic cell's to give (`&tonic free(…)`, not yet a form).\n\nAt the point of each preset that plays it, weight 1, so a query for the mode at one of them finds dorian first, at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from dorian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from dorian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/03-ionian": "---\nid: ionian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(ionian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe major: the key Jambot's composer plays at Ambient's, Bossa nova's and Swing jazz's points (`PRESETS`' `mode`, yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/style.ts).\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic D`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole: there is no default, since a default tonic plays a wrong key silently (#117); the performer's room, `free(…)`, is the tonic cell's to give (`&tonic free(…)`, not yet a form).\n\nAt the point of each preset that plays it, weight 1, so a query for the mode at one of them finds ionian first, at distance 0.\nThe bell and scale (`05-bell-and-scale.md`) is ionian too, elsewhere.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from ionian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from ionian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/04-mixolydian": "---\nid: mixolydian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.875\n      harm: 0.485\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(mixolydian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe major with a minor seventh: the fourth of the composer's modes (`COMPOSER_MODES`, yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/key.ts), which no preset plays.\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic D`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole: there is no default, since a default tonic plays a wrong key silently (#117); the performer's room, `free(…)`, is the tonic cell's to give (`&tonic free(…)`, not yet a form).\n\nBetween the major and the dorian minor (it shares the major's third and the dorian's seventh), it sits halfway between Funk's point (dorian) and Bossa nova's (ionian), where the son clave 3-2 sits too: the funk and rock of a major key with a flat seventh. It is the nearest mode there only, since each preset's own mode is at distance 0 at its point.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from mixolydian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from mixolydian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/05-bell-and-scale": "---\nid: bell and scale\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.383\n      harm: 0.717\n      artic: 0.25\n      energy: 0.417\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.8\n      harm: 0.1\n      artic: 0.9\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key, &bell, &agogo from &tonic\n&key scale(ionian, &tonic) step=1m*7\n&bell step=&key:pulse &highagogo &highagogo:0:.5 &highagogo:0:.7 &highagogo:0:.5 &highagogo:0:.6 &highagogo:0:.5 &highagogo:0:.7\n&agogo [&bell * .5]\n```\n\nThe West African standard bell pattern, x.x.xx.x.x.x, seven strokes over twelve pulses, has the major scale's intervals, 2 2 1 2 2 2 1 (the example `bell and scale`).\nSo one cell is both: `&key` is the major scale, the piece's main key, and stepped seven times a bar, each step as long as its interval, it is the bell's timeline, which `&bell` strikes (`step=&key:pulse`).\nThe repository's first fragment of two facets, a `mode`, ionian, and a `rhythm`, the bell, each at a place of its own: \"the bell is a world-music associated rhythm-facet and a western music associated harmony / scale-facet\" (the owner, decision 046).\n\nA stepped key that nothing plays doesn't turn, so a line over it (`over=&key`) reads the major scale as `&key scale(ionian, &tonic)` does, note for note; the tonic is left to the text that uses it, `&tonic`, as the mode fragments leave it (#290).\n`step=1m*7` lays the bell over the bar of any meter, as twelve twelfths: over 12/8 they are its pulses, the bell as it is played.\n\nSeven strokes of a high agogô (`&highagogo`, General MIDI's 67, a hole the General MIDI kit fills with its line), the example's accents, at half the level; its mix, `&agogo` (the level, no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291), is none of the drum bars' or the claves', so it layers on any of them.\nAs a rhythm its point is a timeline's: off the beat (sync 0.8), over one static chord (harm 0.1), struck (artic 0.9), steady and fairly dense (energy 0.6), where no preset is.\nAs a mode it is where the major is played: the centroid of the three presets that play ionian, Ambient's, Bossa nova's and Swing jazz's (each axis their mean, to three decimals), where no preset is, so at each of them the plain `ionian` is found first, at distance 0.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key, &bell, &agogo from &tonic`. `&key, &bell, &agogo from \"bell and scale\" D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key, &bell, &agogo from \"bell and scale\"`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/06-harmonic-minor": "---\nid: harmonic minor\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 2c120d4\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(harmonic, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe minor with a raised seventh: the gypsy jazz key of [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md), whose vamp's fifth is then a major chord, a dominant (`[4,6,8]` over D is A C♯ E), and whose line over it is the fifth's phrygian dominant.\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic D`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole, as the other modes leave theirs.\n\nAt a point proposed for an Electro swing preset (sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75), weight 1, Jambot's to adopt (decision 041); Jambot's composer has no harmonic minor among its modes yet (`COMPOSER_MODES`, yggi/jambot packages/engine/src/key.ts).\nAlso at the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1: the key of [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md), its augmented second between the sixth and the seventh the sound of a horror film's minor.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from \"harmonic minor\" D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from \"harmonic minor\"`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/07-phrygian": "---\nid: phrygian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.6\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0.7\n      energy: 0.85\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(phrygian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe minor with a minor second: the flamenco's and metal's mode, its ♭II a semitone above the tonic, a cadence that falls onto it (♭II–i).\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic E`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole, as the other modes leave theirs.\n\nNo preset of Jambot's plays it yet (the owner, 2026-10-29: \"jambot should be able to play all 7 modes. they should all be fragments\", yggi/jambot#516). Placed by hand where it is heard, dark and driven: off the beat, rich, clipped and loud (sync .6, harm .6, artic .7, energy .85), weight 1.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from phrygian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from phrygian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/08-lydian": "---\nid: lydian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.15\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0.15\n      energy: 0.3\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(lydian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe major with a raised fourth: film music's and dream pop's mode, bright and floating, its II a major chord a whole tone above the tonic.\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic E`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole, as the other modes leave theirs.\n\nNo preset of Jambot's plays it yet (yggi/jambot#516). Placed by hand where it is heard, floating: on the beat, rich, legato and quiet (sync .15, harm .6, artic .15, energy .3), weight 1.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from lydian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from lydian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "modes/09-locrian": "---\nid: locrian\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.9\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.9\n    weight: 1\n    facet: mode\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&key from &tonic\n&key scale(locrian, &tonic)\n```\n\nThe mode whose tonic is a diminished chord, its fifth flattened: the least settled of the seven, heard in metal's riffs and in jazz over a half-diminished chord.\nIt defines `&key`, the key (decision 047's interface name, decision 056, named since decision 060), and uses `&tonic`, a cell holding the key's tonic (`&tonic E`, #290), so it fits any workbench that has no key yet and gives the tonic; the harmonies and the bass lines read it (`over=&key`, then `over=&harm`).\nThe tonic is left to the text that uses it, a hole, as the other modes leave theirs.\n\nNo preset of Jambot's plays it yet (yggi/jambot#516). Placed by hand at an edge of the space, frantic: off the beat, the harmony at its richest, clipped and loud (sync .9, harm 1, artic .6, energy .9), weight 1, so no preset's neighbourhood finds it before its own mode.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&key from &tonic`. `&key from locrian D` takes a copy of it, `&tonic` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &key from locrian`, it reads `&tonic` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/01-hook": "---\nid: hook\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&hook from &key\n&hook over=&key step=8n 4 4 3 2@2 ~ 0 2\n```\n\nA pop hook: the fifth twice, stepping down to the third and held, a breath, then the tonic and up a step, so it asks to come round again. Written by hand for Synth-pop's minor (aeolian), its sung, fairly short notes.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&hook`), so `use &hook` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &hook`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Synth-pop's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&hook from &key`. `&hook from hook &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &hook from hook`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/02-octaves": "---\nid: octaves\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&octaves from &key\n&octaves over=&key step=8n 0 ~ 7 ~ 0 0 ~ 7\n```\n\nThe tonic and its octave, struck short on and off the beat: the line a techno track rides a filter over, its pitch all in two notes. Written by hand for Techno, where the harmony stands still and every note is staccato.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&octaves`), so `use &octaves` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &octaves`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Techno's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&octaves from &key`. `&octaves from octaves &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &octaves from octaves`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/03-sigh": "---\nid: sigh\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&sigh from &key\n&sigh over=&key step=8n 4@3 3 2@2 ~ ~\n```\n\nA sigh: the fifth held, falling by step to the third and held again, then two beats of air. Written by hand for Deep house's dorian, a vocal hook's shape over a vamp.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&sigh`), so `use &sigh` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &sigh`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Deep house's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&sigh from &key`. `&sigh from sigh &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &sigh from sigh`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/04-rising": "---\nid: rising\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&rising from &key\n&rising over=&key step=8n 0@2 2@2 4@4\n```\n\nThe triad rising slowly, tonic, third, fifth, the last held half the bar: the owner's own example of a motif's name (#288). Written by hand for Ambient, legato and sparse.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&rising`), so `use &rising` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &rising`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Ambient's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&rising from &key`. `&rising from rising &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &rising from rising`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/05-lazy": "---\nid: lazy\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&lazy from &key\n&lazy over=&key step=8n ~ 2 4 ~ 3@2 2 0\n```\n\nLate in, up to the fifth, then down by step to the tonic, the fourth held: a lazy line behind the beat. Written by hand for Lo-fi hip hop's minor, its swung eighths.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&lazy`), so `use &lazy` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &lazy`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Lo-fi hip hop's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&lazy from &key`. `&lazy from lazy &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &lazy from lazy`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/06-riff": "---\nid: riff\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&riff from &key\n&riff over=&key step=8n 0 ~ 3 0 ~ 4 3 ~\n```\n\nA funk riff: the tonic, the fourth and the fifth, all off and on the beat in short strokes. Written by hand for Funk's dorian, at its most syncopated and staccato.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&riff`), so `use &riff` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &riff`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Funk's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&riff from &key`. `&riff from riff &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &riff from riff`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/07-tresillo": "---\nid: tresillo\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&tresillo from &key\n&tresillo over=&key step=8n 4@3 2@3 0@2\n```\n\nThe fifth, the third and the tonic falling on the tresillo's 3 + 3 + 2. Written by hand for Bossa nova, its melody on the clave's long-long-short.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&tresillo`), so `use &tresillo` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &tresillo`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Bossa nova's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&tresillo from &key`. `&tresillo from tresillo &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &tresillo from tresillo`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/08-bebop": "---\nid: bebop\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bebop from &key\n&bebop over=&key step=8n 0 2 4 6 7@2 6 4\n```\n\nUp the seventh chord to the octave, held, and back down through the seventh: a bebop arpeggio. Written by hand for Swing jazz, where the harmony moves most.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&bebop`), so `use &bebop` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &bebop`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt Swing jazz's point (`presets.ts`), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bebop from &key`. `&bebop from bebop &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &bebop from bebop`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/09-gypsy": "---\nid: gypsy\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 7622a87\n---\n\n```cells\n&gypsy from &key\n&gypsy over=&key step=8n 4 5 6 7@2 6 4@2\n```\n\nThe clarinet's call of [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md): A B♭ C♯ D and back to A in D harmonic minor, the fifth climbing through the minor sixth and the leading note to the octave, gypsy jazz's run.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&gypsy`), so `use &gypsy` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &gypsy`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the point proposed for an Electro swing preset (sync 0.55, harm 0.75, artic 0.6, energy 0.75), as the example's other seeds are: Jambot's to adopt (decision 041).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&gypsy from &key`. `&gypsy from gypsy &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &gypsy from gypsy`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/10-dies-irae": "---\nid: diesIrae\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&diesIrae from &key\n&diesIrae over=&key step=8n 2 1 2 0 1 -1 0@2\n```\n\nThe head of the *Dies irae*, the plainchant of the day of wrath, which Berlioz, Liszt, Saint-Saëns and a century of horror films quote: the third, the second, the third, the tonic, the second, the note below the tonic, and the tonic held (F E F D E C D in D minor; C♯ in harmonic minor, which makes it darker still). The chant is in the public domain.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&diesIrae`), so `use &diesIrae` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &diesIrae`), the line the form moves and answers.\nAt the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1, Jambot's to adopt (decision 041).\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&diesIrae from &key`. `&diesIrae from diesIrae &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &diesIrae from diesIrae`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/11-refrain": "---\nid: refrain\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&refrain from &key\n&refrain over=&key step=8n 2 2 2 4@2 3 2 0\n```\n\nThe refrain under the hook: the third three times, up to the fifth and held, then stepping down home. Written by hand for Synth-pop's minor (aeolian), a sung line that lands where the hook only asks.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&refrain`), so `use &refrain` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &refrain`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Synth-pop's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `hook` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&refrain from &key`. `&refrain from refrain &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &refrain from refrain`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/12-pulse": "---\nid: pulse\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.9\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&pulse from &key\n&pulse over=&key step=8n 0 ~ 0 ~ 2 ~ 0 ~\n```\n\nThe tonic struck on every beat and the third once, all short: a line that is mostly rhythm, as a techno lead is. Written by hand for Techno, where the harmony stands still.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&pulse`), so `use &pulse` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &pulse`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Techno's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `octaves` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&pulse from &key`. `&pulse from pulse &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &pulse from pulse`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/13-soul": "---\nid: soul\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&soul from &key\n&soul over=&key step=8n 4 ~ 4 3 4@2 2@2\n```\n\nThe fifth twice, a turn through the fourth and back, then down to the third and held: a vocal ad lib over a vamp. Written by hand for Deep house's dorian.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&soul`), so `use &soul` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &soul`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Deep house's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `sigh` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&soul from &key`. `&soul from soul &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &soul from soul`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/14-drift": "---\nid: drift\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.3\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&drift from &key\n&drift over=&key step=8n 4@4 3@4\n```\n\nTwo notes, the fifth and the fourth, half a bar each: a line that barely moves, legato and sparse. Written by hand for Ambient.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&drift`), so `use &drift` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &drift`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Ambient's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `rising` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&drift from &key`. `&drift from drift &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &drift from drift`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/15-dusty": "---\nid: dusty\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&dusty from &key\n&dusty over=&key step=8n ~ 0 2 ~ 4 2@3\n```\n\nLate in on the tonic, up through the third to the fifth and back to the third, held to the bar's end: a line that sits behind the beat. Written by hand for Lo-fi hip hop's minor and its swung eighths.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&dusty`), so `use &dusty` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &dusty`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Lo-fi hip hop's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `lazy` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&dusty from &key`. `&dusty from dusty &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &dusty from dusty`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/16-slap": "---\nid: slap\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.85\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&slap from &key\n&slap over=&key step=8n 0 0 ~ 6 0 ~ 4 ~\n```\n\nThe tonic twice, the flat seventh off the beat, the tonic, then the fifth: short and syncopated, the bass player's lick taken up by the lead. Written by hand for Funk's dorian.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&slap`), so `use &slap` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &slap`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Funk's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `riff` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&slap from &key`. `&slap from slap &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &slap from slap`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/17-saudade": "---\nid: saudade\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&saudade from &key\n&saudade over=&key step=8n 2 ~ 3 2 ~ 1 0@2\n```\n\nThe third, the fourth and back, then falling by step to the tonic and held: a sigh between the guitar's chords. Written by hand for Bossa nova.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&saudade`), so `use &saudade` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &saudade`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Bossa nova's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `tresillo` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&saudade from &key`. `&saudade from saudade &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &saudade from saudade`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/18-blue": "---\nid: blue\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.7\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&blue from &key\n&blue over=&key step=8n 4 3 2 1 0@2 -2@2\n```\n\nDown the scale from the fifth to the tonic and on to the sixth below, held: the line that ends a chorus on the sixth. Written by hand for Swing jazz.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&blue`), so `use &blue` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &blue`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Swing jazz's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `bebop` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&blue from &key`. `&blue from blue &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &blue from blue`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/19-lindy": "---\nid: lindy\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.85\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&lindy from &key\n&lindy over=&key step=8n 0@3 4@3 2@2\n```\n\nThe tonic, the fifth and the third on the Charleston's 3 + 3 + 2, as a Lindy hop dances it: the swing era's dance, which electro swing samples. Written by hand for Electro swing's harmonic minor.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&lindy`), so `use &lindy` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &lindy`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Electro swing's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `gypsy` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&lindy from &key`. `&lindy from lindy &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &lindy from lindy`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/20-toll": "---\nid: toll\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&toll from &key\n&toll over=&key step=8n 0@4 -3@4\n```\n\nA bell tolling: the tonic, then the fifth below, half a bar each. Written by hand for Spooky, the knell before the chant.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&toll`), so `use &toll` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &toll`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nNear Spooky's point, 0.1 higher in energy, so a query there finds `diesIrae` first and this one 0.05 away (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&toll from &key`. `&toll from toll &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &toll from toll`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/21-waltz": "---\nid: waltz\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.7\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&waltz from &key\n&waltz over=&key step=8n 0@2 2 4 4@2\n```\n\nThe tonic held on the downbeat, then the third and the fifth, the fifth held into the next bar: a waltz's long first beat and its two light ones.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 3/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&waltz`), so `use &waltz` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &waltz`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 3/4's first point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&waltz from &key`. `&waltz from waltz &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &waltz from waltz`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/22-music-box": "---\nid: musicBox\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.43\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&musicBox from &key\n&musicBox over=&key step=8n 4 3 4 1 2@2\n```\n\nThe fifth, the fourth and the fifth again, then down to the second and the third held: a music box running down, in three. Near Spooky, where 3/4 is found.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 3/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&musicBox`), so `use &musicBox` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &musicBox`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 3/4's point near Spooky (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&musicBox from &key`. `&musicBox from musicBox &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &musicBox from musicBox`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/23-rocking": "---\nid: rocking\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.2\n      artic: 0.2\n      energy: 0\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&rocking from &key\n&rocking over=&key step=8n 0@2 2 4@2 2\n```\n\nLong, short, long, short: a cradle's rock in two groups of three, from the tonic to the fifth and back to the third.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 6/8: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&rocking`), so `use &rocking` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &rocking`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 6/8's first point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&rocking from &key`. `&rocking from rocking &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &rocking from rocking`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/24-sway": "---\nid: sway\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.27\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&sway from &key\n&sway over=&key step=8n 0@3 -1 -2 -1\n```\n\nThe tonic held for half the bar, then a slow wobble down a step, two steps and back: a candle's flame in 6/8. Near Spooky, where 6/8 is found.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 6/8: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&sway`), so `use &sway` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &sway`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 6/8's point near Spooky (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&sway from &key`. `&sway from sway &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &sway from sway`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/25-fivefold": "---\nid: fivefold\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.4\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.3\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&fivefold from &key\n&fivefold over=&key step=8n 0 2 4@4 3 2 1@2\n```\n\nUp the triad to the fifth and held, the bar's first three beats, then down by step through its last two: five beats grouped 3 + 2.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 5/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&fivefold`), so `use &fivefold` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &fivefold`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 5/4's first point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&fivefold from &key`. `&fivefold from fivefold &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &fivefold from fivefold`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/26-limp": "---\nid: limp\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.8\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&limp from &key\n&limp over=&key step=8n 0 ~ 4 ~ 3 2 0\n```\n\nThe tonic, the fifth, then a run down to the tonic: short notes in 7/8's 2 + 2 + 3, the last group the long one.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 7/8: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&limp`), so `use &limp` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &limp`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 7/8's point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&limp from &key`. `&limp from limp &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &limp from limp`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/27-dancer": "---\nid: dancer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.6\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.8\n      energy: 0.9\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&dancer from &key\n&dancer over=&key step=8n 0 ~ 2 4 ~ 5 4 2 1 0\n```\n\nTen eighths as 3 + 3 + 2 + 2: a leap up to the sixth in the threes, then stepping home in the twos.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 10/8: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&dancer`), so `use &dancer` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &dancer`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 10/8's point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&dancer from &key`. `&dancer from dancer &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &dancer from dancer`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/28-shuffle": "---\nid: shuffle\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.7\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&shuffle from &key\n&shuffle over=&key step=8n 0@2 2 3@2 4 4@2 2 0@2 ~\n```\n\nLong, short four times over the bar's four beats: the tonic, the third, the fourth, the fifth and back, a slow blues shuffle in 12/8.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 12/8: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&shuffle`), so `use &shuffle` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &shuffle`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 12/8's point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&shuffle from &key`. `&shuffle from shuffle &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &shuffle from shuffle`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/29-march": "---\nid: march\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0\n      harm: 0.1\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&march from &key\n&march over=&key step=8n 4 4 0 ~\n```\n\nThe fifth twice, then the tonic, and a rest: a march's call, two beats to the bar.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 2/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&march`), so `use &march` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &march`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 2/4's point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&march from &key`. `&march from march &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &march from march`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/30-fanfare": "---\nid: fanfare\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.6\n      artic: 0.9\n      energy: 1\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&fanfare from &key\n&fanfare over=&key step=8n 0 0 0 2@2 4@2 ~\n```\n\nThe tonic three times, then the third and the fifth held: a fanfare's call, in two half-note beats.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4 alla breve: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&fanfare`), so `use &fanfare` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &fanfare`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt 4/4 alla breve's point (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&fanfare from &key`. `&fanfare from fanfare &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &fanfare from fanfare`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/31-question": "---\nid: question\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&question from &key\n&question over=&key step=8n 0 1 2@2 4@4\n```\n\nUp by step to the third, then a leap to the fifth held half the bar: a phrase that ends open, asking for an answer. General-purpose, for any style.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&question`), so `use &question` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &question`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre of style space (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&question from &key`. `&question from question &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &question from question`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/32-reply": "---\nid: reply\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.3\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&reply from &key\n&reply over=&key step=8n 4 3 2@2 0@4\n```\n\nDown by step from the fifth to the third, then home to the tonic held half the bar: the closed answer to `question`. General-purpose.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&reply`), so `use &reply` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &reply`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre, 0.2 lower in energy (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&reply from &key`. `&reply from reply &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &reply from reply`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/33-arpeggio": "---\nid: arpeggio\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&arpeggio from &key\n&arpeggio over=&key step=8n 0 2 4 7 4 2 0 ~\n```\n\nUp the triad to the octave and back down: the plainest line a chord gives. General-purpose, for plainer harmony.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&arpeggio`), so `use &arpeggio` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &arpeggio`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre, 0.2 lower in harmony (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&arpeggio from &key`. `&arpeggio from arpeggio &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &arpeggio from arpeggio`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/34-run": "---\nid: run\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.7\n      artic: 0.5\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&run from &key\n&run over=&key step=8n 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n```\n\nThe scale from the tonic to the octave, one note an eighth: in each mode it walks that mode. General-purpose, for richer harmony.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&run`), so `use &run` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &run`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre, 0.2 higher in harmony (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&run from &key`. `&run from run &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &run from run`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/35-neighbour": "---\nid: neighbour\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&neighbour from &key\n&neighbour over=&key step=8n 0 1 0 -1 0@4\n```\n\nThe tonic, the note above, the tonic, the note below, and the tonic held: the neighbour notes round one pitch. General-purpose, legato.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&neighbour`), so `use &neighbour` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &neighbour`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre, 0.2 lower in articulation (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&neighbour from &key`. `&neighbour from neighbour &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &neighbour from neighbour`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "motifs/36-leap": "---\nid: leap\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.5\n      artic: 0.7\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: motif\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&leap from &key\n&leap over=&key step=8n 0@2 4@2 3 2 1 0\n```\n\nThe tonic, a leap to the fifth, then stepping back down the scale: a leap balanced by steps. General-purpose, short notes.\nIt is a line of degrees of the key (`over=&key`), in eighths, one bar of 4/4: its hole is `&key`, and it taps the host's meter (`step=8n`), with no `&bar`, no voice and no card (#291).\nIts head is named for it (`&leap`), so `use &leap` takes it; a form reads it as its `&call` (`&call step=8n &leap`), the line the form moves and answers.\n\nAt the centre, 0.2 higher in articulation (#369), weight 1, as the facet `motif`.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&leap from &key`. `&leap from leap &key` takes a copy of it, `&key` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &leap from leap`, it reads `&key` by name, as before.\n",
  "performers/01-drums": "---\nid: drums performer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&drums, &drumsOut from (&kit) &drumlines\n&bd, &rim, &sd, &cp, &lt, &hh, &ph, &mt, &oh, &ht, &cr, &rd, &claves from gm_kit\n&kit &bd &rim &sd &cp &lt &hh &ph &mt &oh &ht &cr &rd &claves\n&drumsOut play=&drumlines &kit\n&drums map=role &drumsOut\n```\n\nThe drummer (decisions 058 and 061, #287): a gate, `&drumsOut` (named as Jambot's section text names its gates), whose role is `drums` (`&drums map=role &drumsOut`), playing the part `&drumlines` on 13 of the General MIDI kit's voices, which it takes by name.\nThe part is a stack of lines, one per role, as Jambot's section text writes its drums (yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b, `drumLines`): `&drumlines [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat, &euclid * &euclidLevel]`.\nA gate plays a stack line by line, each as if it were its one line, so every hit still says which line struck it (`kit:voices:kick:…`), the drum role the feel reads (`contracts/feel` v1.1).\nEach line names its own voices, and a hit its level either way, as Strudel has it: its own gain (`&bd:0:.645 ~ ~ &bd`, `s(\"bd:0:.645 ~ ~ bd\")`), or the line times a line of levels in the stack (`&euclid * &euclidLevel`, `s(\"rim(7,16)\").gain(\"…\")`), read at each note's written step, so a straight Euclid under a swung meter keeps its levels, and a number (`&clave * .5`). So the drummer has no level of its own, and its one hole is the score's: `&drumlines`.\nIts kit is the drummer's own set-up of those 13 voices, the kick, the side stick, the snare, the clap, three toms, the closed, pedal and open hats, the crash, the ride and the claves, a table (`&kit`): a line that strikes a voice the kit doesn't hold is an error.\n\nAssociated as the facet `performer` at each of Jambot's eight presets' points (`presets.ts`), at weight 1: every preset's section text plays its drums the same way, on these 13 voices on channel 10, so the eight share this one drummer, and what a preset's drums sound like is its lines, not its player.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&drums, &drumsOut from (&kit) &drumlines`. `&drums from \"drums performer\" &groove` takes a copy of it, `&drumlines` its main argument; `&kit` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"drums performer\"(kit=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &drums from \"drums performer\"`, it reads `&drumlines` by name, as before.\n",
  "performers/02-bass": "---\nid: bass performer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&bass, &bassOut from (&bassLevel) &bassline\n&bassV from bass\n&bassOut play=&bassline^$-12 level=&bassLevel &bassV\n&bass map=role &bassOut\n&bassLevel map=amp .8\n```\n\nThe bass player (decisions 058 and 061): a gate, `&bassOut` (Jambot's section text's name for it), whose role is `bass` (`&bass map=role &bassOut`), playing the part `&bassline` on the `bass` instrument an octave down.\nThe instrument holds the register, `&bassV loop=C2`, and Jambot's section text sounds its bass at C1 (`PIN_VOICES.bass`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so the gate moves the part 12 grid steps down (`^$-12`), and the bass sends the MIDI notes it sends today.\nIts two inputs are the score's (decision 065: the line its main parameter, the level an optional one, one level of .8 by default): `&bassline`, the line (degrees over the chord in force or the key, held and shared as the section text writes them), and `&bassLevel`, its velocities as written: a line of levels (`map=amp step=16n`), or one level where they are all one (`&bassLevel map=amp .8`).\n\nAssociated as the facet `performer` at each of Jambot's eight presets' points (`presets.ts`), at weight 1: every preset's section text plays this part the same way (yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b: one voice, one register and one channel for all eight), so the eight share this one performer, and what a preset sounds like is its parts, not its players.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&bass, &bassOut from (&bassLevel) &bassline`. `&bass from \"bass performer\" &line` takes a copy of it, `&bassline` its main argument; `&bassLevel` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"bass performer\"(bassLevel=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &bass from \"bass performer\"`, it reads `&bassline` by name, as before.\n",
  "performers/03-pad": "---\nid: pad performer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&pad, &padOut from (&padLevel) &padline\n&padV from pad\n&padOut play=&padline level=&padLevel &padV\n&pad map=role &padOut\n&padLevel map=amp .8\n```\n\nThe pad player (decisions 058 and 061): a gate, `&padOut` (Jambot's section text's name for it), whose role is `pad` (`&pad map=role &padOut`), playing the part `&padline` on the `pad` instrument, at its register (`&padV loop=C3`, where Jambot's section text sounds its comp: `PIN_VOICES.comp`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so with no move.\nIts two inputs are the score's (decision 065: the line its main parameter, the level an optional one, one level of .8 by default): `&padline`, the line, and `&padLevel`, its velocities as written, a line of levels or one level.\n\nAssociated as the facet `performer` at each of Jambot's eight presets' points (`presets.ts`), at weight 1: every preset's section text plays this part the same way (yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b: one voice, one register and one channel for all eight), so the eight share this one performer, and what a preset sounds like is its parts, not its players.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&pad, &padOut from (&padLevel) &padline`. `&pad from \"pad performer\" &line` takes a copy of it, `&padline` its main argument; `&padLevel` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"pad performer\"(padLevel=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &pad from \"pad performer\"`, it reads `&padline` by name, as before.\n",
  "performers/04-stab": "---\nid: stab performer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&stab, &stabOut from (&stabLevel) &stabline\n&keysV from keys\n&stabOut play=&stabline level=&stabLevel &keysV\n&stab map=role &stabOut\n&stabLevel map=amp .8\n```\n\nThe stab player (decisions 058 and 061): a gate, `&stabOut` (Jambot's section text's name for it), whose role is `stab` (`&stab map=role &stabOut`), playing the part `&stabline` on the `keys` instrument, at its register (`&keysV loop=C3`, where Jambot's section text sounds its comp: `PIN_VOICES.comp`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so with no move.\nIts two inputs are the score's (decision 065: the line its main parameter, the level an optional one, one level of .8 by default): `&stabline`, the line, and `&stabLevel`, its velocities as written, a line of levels or one level. Jambot sends the pad and the stab on one channel, 3: the score's card puts both gates in one entry (`[&padOut, &stabOut]`).\n\nAssociated as the facet `performer` at each of Jambot's eight presets' points (`presets.ts`), at weight 1: every preset's section text plays this part the same way (yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b: one voice, one register and one channel for all eight), so the eight share this one performer, and what a preset sounds like is its parts, not its players.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&stab, &stabOut from (&stabLevel) &stabline`. `&stab from \"stab performer\" &line` takes a copy of it, `&stabline` its main argument; `&stabLevel` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"stab performer\"(stabLevel=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &stab from \"stab performer\"`, it reads `&stabline` by name, as before.\n",
  "performers/05-lead": "---\nid: lead performer\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: performer\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&lead, &leadOut from (&leadLevel) &leadline\n&leadV from lead\n&leadOut play=&leadline level=&leadLevel &leadV\n&lead map=role &leadOut\n&leadLevel map=amp .8\n```\n\nThe lead player (decisions 058 and 061): a gate, `&leadOut` (Jambot's section text's name for it), whose role is `lead` (`&lead map=role &leadOut`), playing the part `&leadline` on the `lead` instrument, at its register (`&leadV loop=C4`, where Jambot's section text sounds its lead: `PIN_VOICES.lead`, yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b), so with no move.\nIts two inputs are the score's (decision 065: the line its main parameter, the level an optional one, one level of .8 by default): `&leadline`, the line (degrees over the melodic scale or the key), and `&leadLevel`, its velocities as written, a line of levels or one level.\n\nAssociated as the facet `performer` at each of Jambot's eight presets' points (`presets.ts`), at weight 1: every preset's section text plays this part the same way (yggi/jambot `packages/score/src/section-text.ts` @ 24a528b: one voice, one register and one channel for all eight), so the eight share this one performer, and what a preset sounds like is its parts, not its players.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&lead, &leadOut from (&leadLevel) &leadline`. `&lead from \"lead performer\" &line` takes a copy of it, `&leadline` its main argument; `&leadLevel` an optional parameter, its line its default (`\"lead performer\"(leadLevel=…)`). Taken the old way, `use &lead from \"lead performer\"`, it reads `&leadline` by name, as before.\n",
  "rhythms/01-synth-pop-drums": "---\nid: Synth-pop drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.547833 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &bd:0:.536239 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.458553 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.469279 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.161262 &sd:0:.303801 &sd:0:.386943\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.048608 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.278319 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.270073 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.253953 ~ &hh:0:.201438 ~\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Synth-pop (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Synth-pop's point.\n",
  "rhythms/02-techno-drums": "---\nid: Techno drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.763904 ~ ~ ~ &bd:0:.536239 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &bd:0:.524769 ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.607663 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.696633 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.155 &sd:0:.201438 &sd:0:.261951 &sd:0:.321409 ~ &sd:0:.469279 &sd:0:.571393 &sd:0:.632463\n&hat step=16n &hh:0:.367599 &hh:0:.148862 &oh:0:.270073 &hh:0:.148862 &hh:0:.377209 &hh:0:.148862 &oh:0:.278319 &hh:0:.155 &hh:0:.367599 &hh:0:.148862 &oh:0:.278319 &hh:0:.148862 &hh:0:.377209 &hh:0:.148862 &oh:0:.270073 &hh:0:.148862\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &hat]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Techno (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Techno's point.\n",
  "rhythms/03-deep-house-drums": "---\nid: Deep house drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.595449 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &bd:0:.571393 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.502201 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.491103 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.161262 &sd:0:.339513 &sd:0:.406783\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.048608 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n &hh:0:.321409 ~ &hh:0:.253953 ~ &hh:0:.303801 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.286689 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.261951 &hh:0:.094302 &hh:0:.230702 ~\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Deep house (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Deep house's point.\n",
  "rhythms/04-ambient-drums": "---\nid: Ambient drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.513423 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &bd:0:.502201 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.386943 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.458553 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.0992 &sd:0:.136958 &sd:0:.167648 &sd:0:.194432 ~ &sd:0:.303801 &sd:0:.416889 &sd:0:.396801\n&hat step=16n &hh:0:.238328 ~ &hh:0:.174158 ~ &hh:0:.261951 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.230702 ~ &hh:0:.201438 ~ &hh:0:.261951 ~ &hh:0:.2232 ~\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &hat]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Ambient (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Ambient's point.\n",
  "rhythms/05-lo-fi-hip-hop-drums": "---\nid: Lo-fi hip hop drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.524769 ~ ~ &bd:0:.286689 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.458553 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.416889 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.12555 &sd:0:.321409 &sd:0:.358113\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.041912 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.278319 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.253953 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.2232 ~ &hh:0:.215822 ~\n&euclid step=1m &rim(5,16,4)\n&euclidLevel map=amp step=16n .201438 0 0 0 .215822 0 0 .161262 0 0 .230702 0 0 .194432 0 0\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat, &euclid * &euclidLevel]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Lo-fi hip hop (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Lo-fi hip hop's point. The rim's Euclid taps `1m`, and under a swung meter its strokes lean on the sixteenths the meter leans, as the band's rim does (#121).\n",
  "rhythms/06-funk-drums": "---\nid: Funk drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.645049 ~ ~ &bd:0:.386943 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.536239 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.536239 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.180792 &sd:0:.367599 &sd:0:.447951\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.089528 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n &hh:0:.348751 ~ &oh:0:.253953 ~ &hh:0:.330399 &hh:0:.114638 &oh:0:.230702 ~ &hh:0:.312543 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.286689 &hh:0:.104222 &oh:0:.215822 ~\n&euclid step=1m &rim(7,16,0)\n&euclidLevel map=amp step=16n .253953 0 0 .270073 0 .270073 0 .230702 0 0 .278319 0 .270073 0 .295183 0\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat, &euclid * &euclidLevel]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Funk (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Funk's point. The rim's Euclid taps `1m`, and under a swung meter its strokes lean on the sixteenths the meter leans, as the band's rim does (#121).\n",
  "rhythms/07-bossa-nova-drums": "---\nid: Bossa nova drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.502201 ~ ~ &bd:0:.312543 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.416889 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.427119 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.148862 &sd:0:.278319 &sd:0:.348751\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.063488 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.246078 ~ ~ ~ &hh:0:.230702 ~ &hh:0:.18755 ~\n&euclid step=1m &rim(5,16,4)\n&euclidLevel map=amp step=16n .201438 0 0 0 .208568 0 0 .180792 0 0 .215822 0 0 .201438 0 0\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat, &euclid * &euclidLevel]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Bossa nova (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Bossa nova's point.\n",
  "rhythms/08-swing-jazz-drums": "---\nid: Swing jazz drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/jambot packages/score/experiments/drums-in-cells.ts @ 327d6a8\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.559551 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&backbeat step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.416889 ~ ~ ~\n&fill step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.109368 &sd:0:.386943 &sd:0:.367599\n&ghost step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &sd:0:.030008 &sd:0:.0558 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n&hat step=16n &rd:0:.295183 ~ ~ ~ &rd:0:.278319 ~ ~ ~ &rd:0:.230702 ~ ~ ~ &rd:0:.253953 ~ &rd:0:.215822 ~\n&pedal step=16n ~ ~ ~ ~ &ph:0:.161262 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ &ph:0:.201438 ~ ~ ~\n&groove [&kick, &backbeat, &fill, &ghost, &hat, &pedal]\n```\n\nJambot's E31 bar for Swing jazz (yggi/jambot#317): the band's drum part as cells text, without its `&bar` line and its stand-in voices (`&bd s=white` …: the kit fills them, decision 054, rung 2) and its card (its mix is `&groove`, with no `map=midi(10)`: where its notes go is the workbench's and the drummer's, #291), so the host's `&bar`, written first, sets its meter and tempo. At Swing jazz's point.\n",
  "rhythms/09-son-clave-3-2": "---\nid: son clave 3-2\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.875\n      harm: 0.485\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&clave step=16n cycle=2 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!7 &claves ~!3 &claves ~!7\n&percussion [&clave * .5]\n```\n\nThe son clave, 3-2: x..x..x. ..x.x... over two bars of eighths. It is where the bossa nova clave and Funk's Bo Diddley beat come from, and sits halfway between Bossa nova and Funk.\n\nFive strokes of a clave (`&claves`, General MIDI's 75), a sound of its own beside the drum bar's rim, at half the level (velocity 90). `&claves` is a hole, a sound the General MIDI kit fills with the line this fragment used to carry word for word (decision 054, rung 2: #244). Its other names (`&clave`, `&percussion`, its mix at that level, with no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291) are none of the drum bars', so it layers on any of them in one text.\n",
  "rhythms/10-son-clave-2-3": "---\nid: son clave 2-3\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.95\n      harm: 0.35\n      artic: 0.75\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&clave step=16n cycle=2 ~!4 &claves ~!3 &claves ~!7 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!3\n&percussion [&clave * .5]\n```\n\nThe son clave from its other bar, 2-3: it starts off the downbeat, so it sits a step from 3-2 toward Funk, more off the beat and plainer.\n\nFive strokes of a clave (`&claves`, General MIDI's 75), a sound of its own beside the drum bar's rim, at half the level (velocity 90). `&claves` is a hole, a sound the General MIDI kit fills with the line this fragment used to carry word for word (decision 054, rung 2: #244). Its other names (`&clave`, `&percussion`, its mix at that level, with no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291) are none of the drum bars', so it layers on any of them in one text.\n",
  "rhythms/11-rumba-clave-3-2": "---\nid: rumba clave 3-2\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.2\n      artic: 0.75\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&clave step=16n cycle=2 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!7 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!3 &claves ~!7\n&percussion [&clave * .5]\n```\n\nThe rumba clave, 3-2: the son's third stroke an eighth later, off the beat; drums and voices over a static harmony, short and dense: near Funk.\n\nFive strokes of a clave (`&claves`, General MIDI's 75), a sound of its own beside the drum bar's rim, at half the level (velocity 90). `&claves` is a hole, a sound the General MIDI kit fills with the line this fragment used to carry word for word (decision 054, rung 2: #244). Its other names (`&clave`, `&percussion`, its mix at that level, with no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291) are none of the drum bars', so it layers on any of them in one text.\n",
  "rhythms/12-bossa-nova-clave": "---\nid: bossa nova clave\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.8\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&clave step=16n cycle=2 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!7 &claves ~!5 &claves ~!5\n&percussion [&clave * .5]\n```\n\nThe bossa nova clave: the son's last stroke an eighth later. Bossa nova's harmony and articulation, a little more off the beat and sparser than its drum bar: five strokes in two bars.\n\nFive strokes of a clave (`&claves`, General MIDI's 75), a sound of its own beside the drum bar's rim, at half the level (velocity 90). `&claves` is a hole, a sound the General MIDI kit fills with the line this fragment used to carry word for word (decision 054, rung 2: #244). Its other names (`&clave`, `&percussion`, its mix at that level, with no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291) are none of the drum bars', so it layers on any of them in one text.\n",
  "rhythms/13-bossa-nova-clave-one-bar": "---\nid: bossa nova clave (one bar)\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.8\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&clave step=16n &claves ~!2 &claves ~!2 &claves ~!3 &claves ~!2 &claves ~!2\n&percussion [&clave * .5]\n```\n\nThe bossa nova clave in one bar of sixteenths, x..x..x...x..x..: as dense as Bossa nova's drum bar, written in the same sixteenths, so at Bossa nova's energy; off the beat as the two-bar one. Which of the two fits a composition is the fit's to choose (#144), not the association's.\n\nFive strokes of a clave (`&claves`, General MIDI's 75), a sound of its own beside the drum bar's rim, at half the level (velocity 90). `&claves` is a hole, a sound the General MIDI kit fills with the line this fragment used to carry word for word (decision 054, rung 2: #244). Its other names (`&clave`, `&percussion`, its mix at that level, with no card: where its notes go is the workbench's, #291) are none of the drum bars', so it layers on any of them in one text.\n",
  "rhythms/14-electro-swing-drums": "---\nid: Electro swing drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 2c120d4\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=4n &bd!4\n&clap step=4n ~ &cp:0:.6 ~ &cp:0:.6\n&hats step=8n ~ &oh:0:.4 ~ &oh:0:.4 ~ &oh:0:.4 ~ &oh:0:.4\n&ticks step=16n &hh:0:.2 &hh:0:.2? &hh:0:.2 &hh:0:.2?.7 &hh:0:.2 &hh:0:.2? &hh:0:.2 [&hh:0:.2,&sd:0:.03]\n&groove [&kick, &clap, &hats, &ticks]\n```\n\nThe electro swing beat of [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md): house's four on the floor and its clap on two and four, under a jazz record's swung eighths, the open hat on every off-beat and a sixteenth hat with some strokes left to chance (`?`, keyed on the seed: decision 031) and a ghost of the snare on the last.\nIt holds no `&bar`, so the host's meter swings it: under `4/4 swung on 8n` (or the example's lighter `swing=8n:.64`) the open hats fall late, the kick and the clap stay on the beat.\nIts lines strike the kit's names (`&bd` `&cp` `&oh` `&hh` `&sd`), holes the General MIDI kit fills, and carry no card (#291): `&groove` is the mix, its levels in the hits.\nA piece arranging it takes its limbs by name (`use &kick, &clap, &hats, &ticks from \"Electro swing drums\"`), as the example does, each under a level of its own.\n\nAt a point proposed for an Electro swing preset (sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75), weight 1: no preset of Jambot's sits there yet, and the axes are Jambot's (decision 041), so the point is this file's, Jambot's to adopt.\n",
  "rhythms/15-spooky-drums": "---\nid: Spooky drums\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: rhythm\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&kick step=16n &bd:0:.55 &bd:0:.3 ~ ~\n&hat step=4n &rd:0:.12\n&euclid step=1m [~ &rim]\n&groove [&kick, &hat, &euclid * .25]\n```\n\nA heartbeat, a clock and a knock: the beat of [Spooky, in pieces](../../examples/spooky.md).\nThe kick is a heartbeat on every beat, its second stroke a sixteenth after the first and softer (lub-dub); the ride ticks each beat, faint, a clock; the rim knocks once, at the middle of the bar, where the heart is between beats in a bar of an odd number of them.\nEvery line fits any meter and lands on its sixteenths: the kick and the ride cycle on a beat (`step=16n` four long, `step=4n` one long), and the rim halves the bar (`step=1m [~ &rim]`), and half of every bar the library's meters make is a whole number of sixteenths (6 in 3/4, 10 in 5/4, 7 in 7/8), so in 5/4 the heart beats five times and the knock falls between the third beat's strokes.\nA Euclid spread over the bar (`step=1m &rim(3,8)`, v0.12.0's) put the knocks between the sixteenths of any bar but 4/4's and 12/8's, where a reader on the bar's sixteenths, as Jambot's drummer is, can't play them; a line on eighths (`step=8n`) lands on them but laps a bar of 4/4, which the fit refuses under the other meters.\nIts lines are named by Jambot's drum roles (`kick`, `hat`, `euclid`) and strike only voices its kit holds (`&bd` 36, `&rd` 51, `&rim` 37), so the drummer plays it as it is; they strike the kit's names, holes the General MIDI kit fills, and carry no card (#291): `&groove` is the mix.\nWritten by hand for the point proposed for a Spooky preset (sync .2, harm .9, artic .3, energy .35; #349), weight 1: no preset of Jambot's sits there yet, and the axes are Jambot's (decision 041), so the point is this file's, Jambot's to adopt.\n",
  "stab/01-charleston-stabs": "---\nid: Charleston stabs\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: stab\nsource: seed\nlifted: yggi/cells examples/electroswing.md @ 2c120d4\n---\n\n```cells\n&stabline from &harm\n&stabline step=8n cycle=4 &charleston!3 &push\n&charleston over=&harm step=8n [0,1,2] ~ ~ [0,1,2] ~@4\n&push over=&harm step=8n [0,1,2] ~ ~ [0,1,2] ~ [0,1,2] ~ &ahead\n&ahead over=&harm[>>] [1,2,3]\n```\n\nThe stabs of [Electro swing, in pieces](../../examples/electroswing.md): the Charleston, a chord on one and on the and of two, three bars, and a fourth that pushes: its last stab, on the and of four, is the next chord, its third and fifth with its root on top (`&ahead over=&harm[>>]`, as the funk bass anticipates with `&bassNext`).\nIt is the part the stab performer plays (`&stabline`, decision 058), the first of the facet `stab`, as the bass lines are the bass performer's: its chords are indices into the chord in force (`over=&harm`), so its holes are `&harm` and a meter, and its velocities are the performer's (`&stabLevel`).\n`&charleston`, `&push` and `&ahead` are its helpers: `use &stabline from \"Charleston stabs\"` takes them.\nIt is the example's line at the commit it was lifted from, but for that last stab, which there read the chord in force (the owner's review of #305).\n\nAt a point proposed for an Electro swing preset (sync .55, harm .75, artic .6, energy .75), weight 1: no preset of Jambot's sits there yet, and the axes are Jambot's (decision 041), so the point is this file's, Jambot's to adopt.\n\n**Its signature** (decision 065): `&stabline from &harm`. `&stabline from \"Charleston stabs\" &harm` takes a copy of it, `&harm` its main argument. Taken the old way, `use &stabline from \"Charleston stabs\"`, it reads `&harm` by name, as before.\n",
  "styles/01-styles": "---\nid: styles\nassociation:\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.3\n      harm: 0.45\n      artic: 0.55\n      energy: 0.55\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.12\n      harm: 0\n      artic: 1\n      energy: 0.8\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 0.55\n      artic: 0.65\n      energy: 0.65\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.05\n      harm: 0.3\n      artic: 0\n      energy: 0.2\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.5\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.35\n      energy: 0.5\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 1\n      harm: 0.12\n      artic: 0.85\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.75\n      harm: 0.85\n      artic: 0.45\n      energy: 0.45\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.35\n      harm: 1\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.6\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.55\n      harm: 0.75\n      artic: 0.6\n      energy: 0.75\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\n  - point:\n      sync: 0.2\n      harm: 0.9\n      artic: 0.3\n      energy: 0.35\n    weight: 1\n    facet: style\nsource: seed\n---\n\n```cells\n&synthPop map=style sync=.3 harm=.45 artic=.55 energy=.55\n&techno map=style sync=.12 harm=0 artic=1 energy=.8\n&deepHouse map=style sync=.35 harm=.55 artic=.65 energy=.65\n&ambient map=style sync=.05 harm=.3 artic=0 energy=.2\n&lofi map=style sync=.5 harm=.75 artic=.35 energy=.5\n&funk map=style sync=1 harm=.12 artic=.85 energy=.75\n&bossaNova map=style sync=.75 harm=.85 artic=.45 energy=.45\n&swingJazz map=style sync=.35 harm=1 artic=.3 energy=.6\n&electroSwing map=style sync=.55 harm=.75 artic=.6 energy=.75\n&spooky map=style sync=.2 harm=.9 artic=.3 energy=.35\n```\n\nThe styles of Jambot's ten presets (decision 063 §3, #391), each a `map=style` cell at the point the preset plays, its axes by name (cells' table of axes, `AXES`): the eight of the prototype, then Electro swing and Spooky (#349). A score names its section's style by one of them where the section sits exactly on it, and by its numbers or a mix of them where it doesn't:\n\n```text\n&funk from styles\n&style label=\"Funk\" style=&funk\n```\n\nThe default band reads the style through `&style` (`band`: its bass's and its lead's cutoff), and so does its choice of instruments (`resolveBand`): Spooky's, named, plays the round bass, the organ, the celesta and the theremin, as its numbers do.\n\nThe points are Jambot's (`src/repository/presets.ts`, lifted from yggi/jambot `packages/engine/src/style.ts`), and a test holds the two to each other. Associated once at each of them, as the facet `style`, at weight 1: the style nearest a point is a query (`{ facet: 'style' }`).\n",
};
